#====================================================================
# E544 draft — filled by adaptation run (libasd 1.5.6, OHOS PC)
#====================================================================
id:                     E544
trigger_tool:           cmake
phase:                  configuration
error_signature:        all the tests are disabled|:BOOL=OFF.*TESTS|0 tests.*out of 0|Test #.*not found without any test
severity:               3
category:               cmake, build-system, detection
match_keywords:         option, cmake, LIBASD_BUILD_TESTS, tests disabled, silent, default off, enable_testing
title:                  cmake option() without a description string silently disables the feature it enables
root_cause:             CMake requires option(<variable> "description" [<value>]); with only two arguments the second token is parsed as the description and the cache variable defaults to OFF. An upstream line like option(LIBASD_BUILD_TESTS ON) therefore leaves tests disabled by default even though the source reads as "ON": the tests subdirectory is never added, ctest registers 0 tests, and configure/build exit 0 — a silent false green. The false green is compounded when a message(WARNING) about missing Boost looks like the cause, while the option() call is the real gate.
affected_scope:         Any CMake project calling option(NAME ON/OFF) without a quoted description; auditors counting tests from CMake source must verify the effective cache value instead of trusting the literal argument
verification_cmd:       cmake -S . -B build -DNAME=ON && grep "NAME:BOOL" build/CMakeCache.txt
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           pass-explicit-dashd-and-fix-option-signature
rec_description:        Two independent fixes: (1) when building, pass the flag explicitly (-DNAME=ON) so the behavior does not depend on the malformed option() call; (2) patch option(NAME ON) to option(NAME "Build ..." ON) with a real description so upstream defaults match the documented intent. Then assert the registered test count is nonzero before trusting ctest output.
rec_command:            grep -nE 'option\([A-Za-z_]+ (ON|OFF|TRUE|FALSE)\)' CMakeLists.txt src/*/CMakeLists.txt
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               explicit-cache-variable-plus-option-patch
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      count-registered-tests-as-gate
fallback_description:   If the option() patch is out of scope, at minimum fail the verification when ctest reports 0 registered tests while static analysis shows test targets exist, so the false green cannot propagate.
fallback_command:       ctest -N | tee; test "$(ctest -N | grep -c 'Test #')" -gt 0
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          nonzero-test-count-gate
forbid_1_pattern:       set\(LIBASD_BUILD_TESTS OFF\)|-DLIBASD_BUILD_TESTS=OFF
forbid_1_reason:        Disabling the tests instead of fixing the option() signature produces exactly the silent skip the entry documents.
forbid_1_consequence:   Upstream suite numbers shrink to 0 without an honest skip record.
principles:             P002,P014
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:             E321
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E544-draft-E961.md
last_updated:           2026-09-05
source_event:           libasd 1.5.6 OHOS upstream Boost.Test run (LIBASD_BUILD_TESTS:BOOL=OFF discovery)
authors:                wanderlust_0823
source_pr:              7929
source_commit:          none
metrics_success_count:  0
metrics_fail_count:     0
